Vendored data and its licenses
==============================

The mysterynpi package itself is MIT (see LICENSE). It vendors three data
artifacts from other sources, each rebuilt by a pinned script in data-raw/:

NICKNAME_EDGES
  Source:  https://github.com/carltonnorthern/nicknames (names.csv)
  License: Apache License 2.0 -- full text: inst/nicknames-LICENSE
  Script:  data-raw/NICKNAME_EDGES.R (pinned commit recorded there)

WINKLER_CENSUS
  Source:  https://github.com/TeamCohen/secondstring (data/censusText.txt);
           synthetic census pairs authored by William Winkler and
           distributed with the SecondString project (Cohen, Ravikumar &
           Fienberg, 2003)
  License: Carnegie Mellon University, 2003 -- permissive with notice
           retention; full text: inst/secondstring-LICENSE
  Script:  data-raw/WINKLER_CENSUS.R (pinned commit recorded there)

SURNAME_FREQUENCIES
  Source:  U.S. Census Bureau, "Frequently Occurring Surnames from the
           2010 Census",
           https://www.census.gov/topics/population/genealogy/data/2010_surnames.html
  License: U.S. government work, public domain
  Script:  data-raw/SURNAME_FREQUENCIES.R

ROSTER_BENCHMARK is authored with this package (data-raw/ROSTER_BENCHMARK.R)
and carries the package's MIT license; its surnames are drawn from the
public-domain Census file above and no row describes a real person.
